ted":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible on 4.8.dev3\n- Reproducible on 4.7.1.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.8.dev3 - Android 16 (SDK 36 build OS3.0.301.0.WOJEUXM) - Single-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Mobile) - integrated Mali-G720 MC7 - MT6899 (8 threads) - Android (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe minimum size of the Shader Editor is too big, causing problems like this on small screens: (bottom bar hidden)\n\n<img width=\"2048\" height=\"921\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8fd26285-f252-4870-8e03-e3217e29fbdf\" />\n\nThis is especially bad as on master the automatic Editor Scale has increased yet again...\n\nBasically, I would prefer if the minimum size would be smaller, but the default size stay as it is (like many other bottom dock tabs do - small minimum size, but they open big by default)\n\nMinimum size of the audio tab:\n<img width=\"1345\" height=\"163\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/eac3b759-b97d-4130-9e92-04e2eae5cbb1\" />\n\nDefault size:\n<img width=\"1313\" height=\"519\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a92f9e0d-ed63-4f06-93f3-f3d461c7f566\" />\n\nI know that this isn't applicable to text editors, but I hope you get the general idea.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open the Shader Editor\n\nTo recreate the issue in the screenshot:\n1. Set the Editor Scale to a high number (needs to be balanced, not too big, not too small)\n2. Open the Script Editor\n3. Open the Shader Editor\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"NoNormalDev","id":190293561,"node_id":"U_kgDOC1emOQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/190293561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev","html_url":"https://github.com/NoNormalDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com